TIP:  The opening riff is a little awkward.  You play the second chord and then pick the note.  If untransposed it's a (D) followed by two (Am7)s and then you pick note <a> at the 1st string of the 5th fret (actually the 7th fret with capo 2) with a gently upstroke.  There's no easy way to pick that 1st string so you just come off the (Am7) and get to it the best you can and then go back for the next (D).

TIP:  The above pattern also permeates the song but a variation.  You don't play the (a) note again but instead play one (Am7) and then an (Am) which will include a middle register (a) as a substitute.  If this is too messy you can also just play two (Am7)s or two (Am)s.  Finally, notice the pattern breaks at the end of the song.  Just follow the chords.  And remember to lower your voice going into the bridge to match the (Em).  Groovy. 
 
       
